.TH SWAYDESK-OSD-BAR 1 2026-11-14 "swaydesk 0.1.3" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-osd\-bar \- volume and brightness indicator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-osd\-bar
.SH DESCRIPTION
A resident, hidden window that shows the volume or brightness level for a second, above the dock, when sway\-osd changes it. sway\-osd writes the state to $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sway\-osd\-bar.state and sends SIGUSR1 to this process. A theme change ends it, and the Sway configuration starts it again.
.PP
The session runs it under the name sway\-osd\-bar (a link in the package's helper directory to /usr/bin/swaydesk\-osd\-bar); the process name is sway\-osd\-bar too.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 at once without doing anything: the Python launchers use it to check that the binary and its libraries load.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sway\-osd\-bar.state
The level to show.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sway\-osd\-bar.pid
The process to signal.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sway\-desktop/config.toml
The desktop configuration: language, accent color, GTK and icon themes, folder color, file manager, weather location and holidays.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sway (5),
.BR swaydesk (7)
